[{:db/id "q-104871/selection/274794e486a078281de48e6eda0f1321143363497dc9943b66c4feec85e3519a" :answer/id #uuid "421c358a-2a34-5df1-a3f4-ea24e97b071a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4t-3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-104871/selection/57b633eb8e218bed41d719b76bf2d6ca8d0a62a346696fea037e875af663ee4e" :answer/id #uuid "a2a10e03-901e-5e5d-bc2c-d409a4634315" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-4t+3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-104871/selection/3a64501f7dfc50de6bce1f0d2666613750b8d170c1449ee83b8b4bfadae87ecc" :answer/id #uuid "57c16c71-d785-55a7-badc-dd726531e6ff" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "8t-6" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-104871/selection/ad9e8e300c6c9c42103f683a2bc995fcaf76d9db4a64b49b125f40e411895d60" :answer/id #uuid "7345c84e-0bf3-5007-85a9-02e8206cf377" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-8t+6" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-104871/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" :answer/id #uuid "b7fb3eea-a71a-5f62-98d2-a7fc0d9810ae" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-104871/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "f2e21f82-f24f-5792-b857-183cfbb32c2b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-104871/selection/274794e486a078281de48e6eda0f1321143363497dc9943b66c4feec85e3519a" :answer-field/choices ["q-104871/selection/274794e486a078281de48e6eda0f1321143363497dc9943b66c4feec85e3519a" "q-104871/selection/57b633eb8e218bed41d719b76bf2d6ca8d0a62a346696fea037e875af663ee4e" "q-104871/selection/3a64501f7dfc50de6bce1f0d2666613750b8d170c1449ee83b8b4bfadae87ecc" "q-104871/selection/ad9e8e300c6c9c42103f683a2bc995fcaf76d9db4a64b49b125f40e411895d60" "q-104871/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-104871" :question/id #uuid "37ca62b1-ea69-5fd7-b661-830063f158d1" :question/math-academy-id "q-104871" :question/problem "Let $V={R}_{1}[t],$ the vector space of real polynomials of degree at most $1,$ and let the inner product on $V$ be defined as\n\n$$\n⟨p(t),q(t)⟩=p(0)q(0)+p(1)q(1).\n$$\n\nNow consider the following elements of $V:$\n\n$$\n{p}_{1}(t)=2t,\\,{p}_{2}(t)=t-1,\\,q(t)=4t-3\n$$\n\nFind the orthogonal projection of $q(t)$ onto $S=\\text{Span}{{p}_{1}(t),{p}_{2}(t)}$ given that ${p}_{1}(t)⊥{p}_{2}(t)$ with respect to the inner product, and that the orthogonal projection of $q(t)$ onto $\\text{Span}{{p}_{1}(t)}$ equals $t.$" :question/worked-solution "Since the set ${{p}_{1}(t),{p}_{2}(t)}$ is orthogonal, the orthogonal projection of $q(t)$ onto the subspace $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{\\text{proj}}_{S}\\,q(t)={\\text{proj}}_{{p}_{1}(t)}\\,q(t)+{\\text{proj}}_{{p}_{2}(t)}\\,q(t).\n$$\n\nWe are given that ${\\text{proj}}_{{p}_{1}(t)}\\,q(t)=t,$ so let's now find the orthogonal projection of $q(t)$ onto $\\text{Span}{{p}_{2}(t)}.$ This can be computed as\n\n$$\n{\\text{proj}}_{{p}_{2}(t)}\\,q(t)=\\frac{⟨q(t),{p}_{2}(t)⟩}{⟨{p}_{2}(t),{p}_{2}(t)⟩}\\,{p}_{2}(t).\n$$\n\n \n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨q(t),{p}_{2}(t)⟩ & =q(0){p}_{2}(0)+q(1){p}_{2}(1) \\\\  & =(4t-3){|}_{0}\\cdot (t-1){|}_{0}+(4t-3){|}_{1}\\cdot (t-1){|}_{1} \\\\  & =(-3)\\cdot (-1)+1\\cdot 0 \\\\  & =3,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n  \n\nand\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨{p}_{2}(t),{p}_{2}(t)⟩ & ={p}_{2}(0){p}_{2}(0)+{p}_{2}(1){p}_{2}(1) \\\\  & =(t-1)^{2}{|}_{0}+(t-1)^{2}{|}_{1} \\\\  & =(-1)^{2}+{0}^{2} \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n  \n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{{p}_{2}(t)}\\,q(t) & =\\frac{3}{1}\\cdot (t-1)=3t-3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n  \n\nFinally,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{S}\\,q(t) & ={\\text{proj}}_{{p}_{1}(t)}\\,q(t)+{\\text{proj}}_{{p}_{2}(t)}\\,q(t) \\\\  & =t+(3t-3) \\\\  & =4t-3.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-104871/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "39692b40-7d68-5ae5-9fe1-0f8b0b2e0d77"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-104871"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-104894/selection/b406c6c83e0452b915ea9d7412171b62f194f19481e7423ffa2d5db1ef001167" :answer/id #uuid "fd4ae18a-7244-5381-bb06-c8e7522a00af" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{t}^{2}+t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-104894/selection/cb9ad14c4d0189695cf5d02baf58f5eec7ac941edc170f6dffed142cbab880f5" :answer/id #uuid "8e5bfb0c-7895-5abe-af6a-f610e22ffe36" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{t}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-104894/selection/5703ee2d54fb35f67e70e698e3bd6d35f8014756f60fa8ceb8ec12784e7ec969" :answer/id #uuid "95ed8383-cd42-5418-9860-9d09884bad32" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{t}^{2}-t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-104894/selection/b4ac6936776440214aaebffba73d7fd5fde48538e542fa8a6de8788032995d2c" :answer/id #uuid "dc2b862c-8b0a-5f41-ae03-b6e8fc993588" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-104894/selection/eaba4da4447c9b33a895d609a3f81feab98b794b9799550831cc4a744e96cb0d" :answer/id #uuid "e1573851-3592-5352-ab86-3c00eb385611" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "t-1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-104894/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "c9da03e5-022a-5795-a16e-83c330c668d3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-104894/selection/b4ac6936776440214aaebffba73d7fd5fde48538e542fa8a6de8788032995d2c" :answer-field/choices ["q-104894/selection/b406c6c83e0452b915ea9d7412171b62f194f19481e7423ffa2d5db1ef001167" "q-104894/selection/cb9ad14c4d0189695cf5d02baf58f5eec7ac941edc170f6dffed142cbab880f5" "q-104894/selection/5703ee2d54fb35f67e70e698e3bd6d35f8014756f60fa8ceb8ec12784e7ec969" "q-104894/selection/b4ac6936776440214aaebffba73d7fd5fde48538e542fa8a6de8788032995d2c" "q-104894/selection/eaba4da4447c9b33a895d609a3f81feab98b794b9799550831cc4a744e96cb0d"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-104894" :question/id #uuid "a000c0ed-36b2-53a6-9bbc-b17fbc56e03d" :question/math-academy-id "q-104894" :question/problem "Let $V={R}_{2}[t],$ the vector space of real polynomials of degree at most $2,$ and let the inner product on $V$ be defined as\n\n$$\n⟨p(t),q(t)⟩=p(-1)q(-1)+p(0)q(0)+p(1)q(1).\n$$\n\nNow consider the following elements of $V:$\n\n$$\n{p}_{1}(t)=t,\\,{p}_{2}(t)={t}^{2}-1,\\,q(t)={t}^{2}+t\n$$\n\nFind the orthogonal projection of $q(t)$ onto $S=\\text{Span}{{p}_{1}(t),{p}_{2}(t)}$ given that ${p}_{1}(t)⊥{p}_{2}(t)$ with respect to the inner product, and that the orthogonal projection of $q(t)$ onto $\\text{Span}{{p}_{2}(t)}$ equals $0.$" :question/worked-solution "Since the set ${{p}_{1}(t),{p}_{2}(t)}$ is orthogonal, the orthogonal projection of $q(t)$ onto the subspace $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{\\text{proj}}_{S}\\,q(t)={\\text{proj}}_{{p}_{1}(t)}\\,q(t)+{\\text{proj}}_{{p}_{2}(t)}\\,q(t).\n$$\n\nWe are given that ${\\text{proj}}_{{p}_{2}(t)}\\,q(t)=0,$ so let's now find the orthogonal projection of $q(t)$ onto $\\text{Span}{{p}_{1}(t)}.$ This can be computed as\n\n$$\n{\\text{proj}}_{{p}_{1}(t)}\\,q(t)=\\frac{⟨q(t),{p}_{1}(t)⟩}{⟨{p}_{1}(t),{p}_{1}(t)⟩}\\,{p}_{1}(t).\n$$\n\n \n\nIn our case, we have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨q(t),{p}_{1}(t)⟩ & =q(-1){p}_{1}(-1)+q(0){p}_{1}(0)+q(1){p}_{1}(1) \\\\  & =({t}^{2}\\,+\\,t){|}_{-1}\\,\\,\\cdot \\,(t){|}_{-1}+({t}^{2}\\,+\\,t){|}_{0}\\,\\,\\cdot \\,(t){|}_{0}+({t}^{2}\\,+\\,t){|}_{1}\\,\\,\\cdot \\,(t){|}_{1} \\\\  & =0\\cdot (-1)+0\\cdot 0+2\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =2,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n  \n\nand\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨{p}_{1}(t),{p}_{1}(t)⟩ & ={p}_{1}(-1){p}_{1}(-1)+{p}_{1}(0){p}_{1}(0)+{p}_{1}(1){p}_{1}(1) \\\\  & =(t)^{2}{|}_{-1}+(t)^{2}{|}_{0}+(t)^{2}{|}_{1} \\\\  & =(-1)^{2}+{0}^{2}+{1}^{2} \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n  \n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{{p}_{1}(t)}\\,q(t) & =\\frac{2}{2}\\cdot t=t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n  \n\nFinally,  \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{S}\\,q(t) & ={\\text{proj}}_{{p}_{1}(t)}\\,q(t)+{\\text{proj}}_{{p}_{2}(t)}\\,q(t) \\\\  & =t+0 \\\\  & =t.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-104894/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "39692b40-7d68-5ae5-9fe1-0f8b0b2e0d77"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-104894"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-105100/selection/f7d9e6eb81bd5ccedfb80cadb99821eb93db977c7de84fe50ed563f066c51ac6" :answer/id #uuid "3cc9f1ba-df54-5452-8133-e2f92cea7d38" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{t}^{2}+1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-105100/selection/9dc6be64be00e3179ace4ce11342edde6381b848d1a1e150855c73ae63443903" :answer/id #uuid "3a029d30-65ce-5da7-898a-807f426293b6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{t}^{2}+6t+1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-105100/selection/7b33cb6796e81c3aec7cace2bb77f74e6a29c84f435a74c92cb4963ca11e527c" :answer/id #uuid "e5ea22ac-9ebf-520c-b2db-39a29c4be6de" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "10{t}^{3}+3t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-105100/selection/77baf6fcc8dc4d610efea7557c3e7a0eaeff3474a3041467497c38fcb9cf530e" :answer/id #uuid "2e7ceb57-2602-5de7-90ae-5ae6d6bea33d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{t}^{2}-1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-105100/selection/d167a88de8279919cd4426c42b45e96cbe79db72f579f94ad0ef2d59e0ddf3e4" :answer/id #uuid "ca0ba6b4-a699-5c70-9d70-11a98c6feee2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "6t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-105100/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "db39ad06-ef05-5b1f-bbce-49cb36e5b226" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-105100/selection/d167a88de8279919cd4426c42b45e96cbe79db72f579f94ad0ef2d59e0ddf3e4" :answer-field/choices ["q-105100/selection/f7d9e6eb81bd5ccedfb80cadb99821eb93db977c7de84fe50ed563f066c51ac6" "q-105100/selection/9dc6be64be00e3179ace4ce11342edde6381b848d1a1e150855c73ae63443903" "q-105100/selection/7b33cb6796e81c3aec7cace2bb77f74e6a29c84f435a74c92cb4963ca11e527c" "q-105100/selection/77baf6fcc8dc4d610efea7557c3e7a0eaeff3474a3041467497c38fcb9cf530e" "q-105100/selection/d167a88de8279919cd4426c42b45e96cbe79db72f579f94ad0ef2d59e0ddf3e4"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-105100" :question/id #uuid "1f0d026f-9ed8-56c8-b727-7195df6d6021" :question/math-academy-id "q-105100" :question/problem "Let $V=C[-1,1],$ the vector space of continuous functions over $[-1,1]$, and let the inner product on $V$ be defined as\n\n$$\n⟨x(t),y(t)⟩={\\int }_{-1}^{1}x(t)y(t)\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nNow consider the following elements of $V:$ \n\n$$\n{f}_{1}(t)=3t,\\,{f}_{2}(t)={t}^{2}+1,\\,g(t)=10{t}^{3}\n$$\n\nFind the orthogonal projection of $g(t)$ onto $S=\\text{Span}{{f}_{1}(t),{f}_{2}(t)}$ given that ${f}_{1}(t)⊥{f}_{2}(t)$ with respect to the inner product, and that the orthogonal projection of $g(t)$ onto $\\text{Span}{{f}_{1}(t)}$ equals $6t.$" :question/worked-solution "Since the set ${{f}_{1}(t),{f}_{2}(t)}$ is orthogonal, the orthogonal projection of $g(t)$ onto the subspace $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{\\text{proj}}_{S}\\,g(t)={\\text{proj}}_{{f}_{1}(t)}\\,g(t)+{\\text{proj}}_{{f}_{2}(t)}\\,g(t).\n$$\n\nWe are given that ${\\text{proj}}_{{f}_{1}(t)}\\,g(t)=6t,$ so let's now find the orthogonal projection of $g(t)$ onto $\\text{Span}{{f}_{2}(t)}.$ This can be computed as\n\n$$\n{\\text{proj}}_{{f}_{2}(t)}\\,g(t)=\\frac{⟨g(t),{f}_{2}(t)⟩}{⟨{f}_{2}(t),{f}_{2}(t)⟩}\\,{f}_{2}(t).\n$$\n\n \n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨g(t),{f}_{2}(t)⟩ & ={\\int }_{-1}^{1}g(t){f}_{2}(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{1}10{t}^{3}\\cdot ({t}^{2}+1)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{1}10{t}^{3}({t}^{2}+1)\\,\\text{d}t\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that $10{t}^{3}$ is an odd function, while ${t}^{2}+1$ is even. Hence, their product $10{t}^{3}({t}^{2}+1)$ must be an odd function. Now, since we have an integral over the interval $[-1,1],$ which is symmetric about the origin, we can conclude that\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{-1}^{1}10{t}^{3}({t}^{2}+1)\\,\\text{d}t=0.\n$$\n\n  \n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n{\\text{proj}}_{{f}_{2}(t)}\\,g(t)=\\frac{0}{⟨{f}_{2}(t),{f}_{2}(t)⟩}\\cdot ({t}^{2}+1)=0.\n$$\n\nFinally,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{S}\\,g(t) & ={\\text{proj}}_{{f}_{1}(t)}\\,g(t)+{\\text{proj}}_{{f}_{2}(t)}\\,g(t) \\\\  & =6t+0 \\\\  & =6t.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-105100/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "39692b40-7d68-5ae5-9fe1-0f8b0b2e0d77"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-105100"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-105475/selection/73eeaf3fae024b54005d89a5185040ad67cf4b6c72d401d6ad32bf0e79c13de9" :answer/id #uuid "cf9f043d-3361-516b-8021-36c56f671651" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-105475/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" :answer/id #uuid "29c7ce71-e34b-5996-802a-a7f2e068603b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-105475/selection/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54" :answer/id #uuid "2e3ce1ff-36b0-5a98-82ea-604d081f8e97" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-105475/selection/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" :answer/id #uuid "1bc2c36f-9180-5d97-a4bb-ad88e3596d22" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-105475/selection/2edf353dc47d221855e5e7ee4be942392390ff01766e089c29dc368c2051b12d" :answer/id #uuid "ff2f4d72-c5aa-55db-b5f3-979404976304" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-105475/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "0b4b6c59-2046-5d5e-b18d-c297c545a08b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-105475/selection/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" :answer-field/choices ["q-105475/selection/73eeaf3fae024b54005d89a5185040ad67cf4b6c72d401d6ad32bf0e79c13de9" "q-105475/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" "q-105475/selection/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54" "q-105475/selection/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" "q-105475/selection/2edf353dc47d221855e5e7ee4be942392390ff01766e089c29dc368c2051b12d"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-105475" :question/id #uuid "2fb2df70-095b-5b81-a246-2e804ada8ba3" :question/math-academy-id "q-105475" :question/problem "Let $V=C[0,1],$ the vector space of functions that are continuous over $[0,1].$ Given that the inner product on $V$ is defined as \n\n$$\n⟨x(t),y(t)⟩={\\int }_{0}^{1}x(t)y(t)\\,\\text{d}t,\n$$\n\nfind the distance between $f(t)=8t$ and the subspace spanned by $g(t)=4t-2$ with respect to the inner product." :question/worked-solution "The orthogonal projection of $f(t)$ onto $\\text{Span}{g(t)}$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{g(t)}\\,f(t) & =\\frac{⟨f(t),g(t)⟩}{⟨g(t),g(t)⟩}\\,g(t) \\\\  & =\\frac{{\\int }_{0}^{1}8t\\cdot (4t-2)\\,\\text{d}t}{{\\int }_{0}^{1}(4t-2)^{2}\\,\\text{d}t}\\cdot (4t-2) \\\\  & =\\frac{{\\int }_{0}^{1}(32{t}^{2}-16t)\\,\\text{d}t}{{\\int }_{0}^{1}(16{t}^{2}-16t+4)\\,\\text{d}t}\\cdot (4t-2) \\\\  & =\\frac{[\\frac{32}{3}{t}^{3}-8{t}^{2}]_{0}^{1}}{[\\frac{16}{3}{t}^{3}-8{t}^{2}+4t]_{0}^{1}}\\cdot (4t-2) \\\\  & =\\frac{(\\frac{32}{3}-8)-0}{(\\frac{16}{3}-4)-0}\\cdot (6t-3) \\\\  & =\\frac{(\\frac{8}{3})}{(\\frac{4}{3})}\\cdot (4t+2) \\\\  & =2\\cdot (4t-2) \\\\  & =8t-4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe distance between $f(t)=8t$ and the subspace spanned by $g(t)=4t-2$ with respect to our inner product is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d & =‖f(t)-{\\text{proj}}_{g(t)}\\,f(t)‖ \\\\  & =‖8t-(8t-4)‖ \\\\  & =‖4‖ \\\\  & =\\sqrt{⟨4,4⟩}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nComputing the inner product, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨4,4⟩ & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}4\\cdot 4\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}16\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =16t\\,{|}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =16-0 \\\\  & =16.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the distance is $d=\\sqrt{16}=4.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-105475/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "25e84fac-02c3-5111-98b3-bc67fe1ec9ab"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-105475"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-105488/selection/6d0feb8142a7a02fe2f9414f65d24ad6b6e1461293ef76a035b5b31c03d7f658" :answer/id #uuid "e99d78f5-7d23-5860-b726-f770242d40bb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{50}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-105488/selection/5cfe33d704dbba0d7c6cb0e4c8b69c5862cecddd6652e8decd2b6e71b500b63d" :answer/id #uuid "7a22a883-5a19-5879-8980-7727104b6537" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{30}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-105488/selection/3d54f0516e928a95a405b928274c486e572c4630e3e2a40d9da601e3ce2629e1" :answer/id #uuid "7b0b1a26-f579-5840-8668-4b207f166149" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{60}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-105488/selection/5f32bf40eed4f820dc7adb0d04dc4e270f67fa1c88853a1e7b845d5aa68304d4" :answer/id #uuid "d18dac2c-4f62-52b8-a102-0166403e86c8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{40}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-105488/selection/f466a43f43f0dc0ca3002e7c962c946db9590bae749fb49e6d0351f58f25c0d8" :answer/id #uuid "796c4214-08a5-5537-873f-f07374362cf5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{2}0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-105488/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "e9f18baf-03c5-50fe-8c56-32209d6d9081" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-105488/selection/5cfe33d704dbba0d7c6cb0e4c8b69c5862cecddd6652e8decd2b6e71b500b63d" :answer-field/choices ["q-105488/selection/6d0feb8142a7a02fe2f9414f65d24ad6b6e1461293ef76a035b5b31c03d7f658" "q-105488/selection/5cfe33d704dbba0d7c6cb0e4c8b69c5862cecddd6652e8decd2b6e71b500b63d" "q-105488/selection/3d54f0516e928a95a405b928274c486e572c4630e3e2a40d9da601e3ce2629e1" "q-105488/selection/5f32bf40eed4f820dc7adb0d04dc4e270f67fa1c88853a1e7b845d5aa68304d4" "q-105488/selection/f466a43f43f0dc0ca3002e7c962c946db9590bae749fb49e6d0351f58f25c0d8"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-105488" :question/id #uuid "ca703624-c22b-5cc8-9120-0825031366fc" :question/math-academy-id "q-105488" :question/problem "Let $V={R}_{2}[t],$ the vector space of polynomials of degree at most $2$ with real coefficients. Given that the inner product on $V$ is defined as \n\n$$\n⟨p(t),q(t)⟩=p(-1)q(-1)+p(0)q(0)+p(1)q(1),\n$$\n\nfind the distance between $p(t)=5t$ and the subspace spanned by $q(t)=t-1$ with respect to the inner product." :question/worked-solution "The orthogonal projection of $p(t)$ onto $\\text{Span}{q(t)}$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{q(t)}\\,p(t) & =\\frac{⟨p(t),q(t)⟩}{⟨q(t),q(t)⟩}\\,q(t) \\\\  & =\\frac{p(-1)q(-1)+p(0)q(0)+p(1)q(1)}{q(-1)q(-1)+q(0)q(0)+q(1)q(1)}\\cdot q(t) \\\\  & =\\frac{{\\sum }_{i\\in {-1,0,1}}(5t){|}_{t=i}\\cdot (t-1){|}_{t=i}}{{\\sum }_{i\\in {-1,0,1}}(t-1){|}_{t=i}\\cdot (t-1){|}_{t=i}}\\cdot (t-1) \\\\  & =\\frac{(-5)\\cdot (-2)+0\\cdot (-1)+5\\cdot 0}{(-2)\\cdot (-2)+(-1)\\cdot (-1)+0\\cdot 0}\\cdot (t-1) \\\\  & =\\frac{10}{5}\\cdot (t-1) \\\\  & =2(t-1).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nThe distance between $p(t)=5t$ and the subspace spanned by $q(t)=t-1$ with respect to our inner product is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d & =‖p(t)-{\\text{proj}}_{q(t)}\\,p(t)‖ \\\\  & =‖5t-2(t-1)‖ \\\\  & =‖3t+2‖ \\\\  & =\\sqrt{⟨3t+2,3t+2⟩}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nComputing the inner product, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨3t+2,3t+2⟩ & ={\\sum }_{i\\in {-1,0,1}}(3t+2){|}_{t=i}\\cdot (3t+2){|}_{t=i} \\\\  & =(-1)\\cdot (-1)+2\\cdot 2+5\\cdot 5 \\\\  & =1+4+25 \\\\  & =30.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the distance is $d=\\sqrt{30}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-105488/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "25e84fac-02c3-5111-98b3-bc67fe1ec9ab"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-105488"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]}]
